{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 21,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear diligently my speech, and let this be your consolations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Suffer me that I may speak; and after I have spoken, mock on.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my complaint to man? and if ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it were so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", why should not my spirit be troubled?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Mark me, and be astonished, and lay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand upon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even when I remember I am afraid, and trembling taketh hold on my flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why do the wicked live, become old, and, are mighty in power?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their seed is established in their sight with them, and their offspring before their eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their houses ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " safe from fear, neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rod of God upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their bull gendereth, and faileth not; their cow calveth, and casteth not her calf.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They send forth their little ones like a flock, and their children dance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They take the timbrel and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the organ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They spend their days in wealth, and in a moment go down to the grave.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore they say to God, Depart from us; for we desire not the knowledge of thy ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Almighty, that we should serve him? and what profit should we have, if we pray to him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, their good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not in their hand: the counsel of the wicked is far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How oft is the candle of the wicked put out? and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how oft",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cometh their destruction upon them? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " distributeth sorrows in his anger.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are as stubble before the wind, and as chaff that the storm carrieth away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God layeth up his iniquity for his children: he rewardeth him, and he shall know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His eyes shall see his destruction, and he shall drink of the wrath of the Almighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what pleasure ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he in his house after him, when the number of his months is cut off in the midst?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " teach God knowledge? seeing he judgeth those that are high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One dieth in his full strength, being wholly at ease and quiet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His breasts are full of milk, and his bones are moistened with marrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And another dieth in the bitterness of his soul, and never eateth with pleasure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall lie down alike in the dust, and the worms shall cover them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I know your thoughts, and the devices ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye wrongfully imagine against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ye say, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the house of the prince? and where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the dwelling places of the wicked?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have ye not asked them that go by the way? and do ye not know their tokens,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the wicked is reserved to the day of destruction? they will be brought forth to the day of wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who shall declare his way to his face? and who shall repay him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "what",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he hath done?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet he shall be brought to the grave, and shall remain in the tomb.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The clods of the valley will be sweet to him, and every man will draw after him, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " innumerable before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.21.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How then comfort ye me in vain, seeing in your answers there remaineth falsehood?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
